const DAY_REVIEW_READING_GUIDE = "Day review narrative reference\nLocate each phase on the time axis, including the day rollover. Trace actual candles within that phase. Describe the opening-range action, the after-IB expansion or retracement, any failed attempt or regain, and the handoff or final location. Use relative movement when prices are unreadable. Keep the current screenshot's story grounded in its visible candles.\nNew York clocks: Asia IB 19:30–20:30, AIB 20:30–02:00; ATL 02:00–03:00; London IB 03:00–04:00, AIB 04:00–08:30; LTN 08:30–09:30; NY IB 09:30–10:30, AIB 10:30–16:00. NTA uses prior NY 16:00–17:00 and evening 18:00–19:30. The NY forecast starts 08:30; the NY shape starts 09:30.\nKeep three reference frames explicit: phase prose; the full-session formal Narrow/order/close-position code; and location within prior NY BBOX. A rising recovery can stay below BBOX. An early extension can fail, be reclaimed or be reversed in a later phase. Apply formal thresholds only with sufficient exact evidence. Full-day labels and later outcomes are available only after their recorded deadlines.\nLondon L05 is the 03:00–04:00 IB 0.5 extension: upper=IBH+0.5×IB width, lower=IBL−0.5×IB width. This anchor differs from SessionPath full-box range multiples. Preserve touch, completed-close return and endpoint/regain distinctions.\nSource examples below quote Day review Q. Each original screenshot broadly agrees with the narrative; exact formal tags and OHLC were not revalidated. Learn the phase sequence and reference-frame distinctions, and describe the current attached chart from its own evidence.\n2022-01-04 CLG2022, source row 3: “Prior NY recovered. Asia tested above BBOX and returned inside; London dipped then expanded upward. The first upper extension rejected but was reclaimed before08:30. NY expanded higher and finished above the old BBOX.”\n2022-01-07 CLG2022, source row 6: “Asia extended above the old BBOX. London recovered from an early dip but its upside extension did not persist. Selling accelerated into NY; NY traded below the old BBOX and closed just inside its lower edge.”\n2022-01-20 CLH2022, source row 15: “Prior NY ended weak after an upside reversal. NTA and Asia traded below the old low; Asia recovered to the BBOX midpoint before fading. London rotated around the lower edge, made upside extensions and returned to IB. NY rallied above the old high, then reversed through the range and closed below the old low.”\n2022-01-21 CLH2022, source row 16: “Prior NY sold off sharply and weakness continued through NTA. Asia made an early low then recovered. London remained below the prior BBOX and neither0.5 extension was reached by08:30. LTN reclaimed the lower BBOX area; NY retested below, then recovered and balanced inside its lower quarter.”\nJan 7 endpoint caution: the screenshot includes a 16:00-open candle below the old low, while the source inside-close label uses the preceding completed candle. Keep that endpoint distinction unresolved when the required close is unreadable. Assign the 08:30–09:30 selloff to LTN.\nCurrent columns: H/I Asia IB/after-IB; J/K London IB/after-IB; L/M NY IB/after-IB; Q daily story; R formal phase combination; S BBOX endpoint sequence; T timed event tags. Use these headers when an older Researchguide column letter differs.";

